systemd supports auto-mounting the root partition, which simplifies the boot
setup. If this feature is used, the encrypted partition will be made available
at /dev/gpt-auto-root-luks and the unlocked root partition at
/dev/gpt-auto-root.

For auto-mounting to work, the following requirements must be met:
    - the initramfs must use a systemd, not a busybox environment
    - the root and EFI system partitions must be on the same device
    - the correct GPT partition types must be set
    - the boot loader must support auto-mounting

By following this script, all criteria should be met. Nevertheless, you may
still opt to not use this feature if you wish. In that case, the root partition
will be specified explicitly for the kernel on the commandline.
